    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22266" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in-cānus</span></b> , a, um,
		adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>quite gray</i>, <i>hoary</i> (<b>poet.</b> and in post-Aug. prose): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">homo crispus, incanus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Rud. 1, 2, 37</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mentum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					G. 3, 311</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">barba,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					8, 2, 9</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">labra Famis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					8, 804</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caput,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Dom. 20</span></i>
			. —<b>Poet.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">saecula,</span>”
				<i>hoary centuries</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cat.
					95, 6</span></i>
			.</div>
